> > > As I see in the gpsd_config.h file which is generated by scons,
> > > there are several definitions that, as I understand, can be configured during build.
> > > Can anyone tell me how to use the config.in file for that, or any
> > > other way that I can do that?
> > >
> > > For example: I want to enable only NMEA protocol and disable PPS and ntp_shm.
> >
> > Do 'make menuconfig' and go to 'Target packages' -> 'Hardware
> > handling' -> 'gpsd' -> 'Features' and 'Protocols'. The options you
> > mention are called 'NMEA' (under 'Protocols'), 'PPS time syncing
> > support', and 'NTP time hinting support' (both under 'Features').
> > Just enable or disable them as needed.
> >
> > I hope this helps.
